    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1116">

                <pb facs="1188" n="1092" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1092"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Ali Ferrouh Bey.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-10-11"><hi rendition="#italic">October 11,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 11.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging your note of the 11th
                    instant, in which you reply to mine of this date, relative to the refusal of the
                    Turkish consul at New York to visé the passport of the Rev. S. L. Beiler, for
                    use in traveling through Palestine, and inform me that the consul has been
                    directed by wire to visé the passport, I have the honor to thank you for your
                    very prompt and courteous attention to the matter.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
